      "message": "fix(kernel): measure a fan at a spline pole by its true sag\n\nAt a pole of a spline face every u is the same point, so the planner\ngives the apex node any u. The deviation measure interpolated u from\nthat value across half the period inside each fan triangle, projected\nfrom a hint on the far side, and judged a good mesh 0.3-0.5 mm off its\nsurface. The QA mould q02 (ellipsoid boss) was refused at import.\n\nmesh_pole::settle moves the free parameter of a corner on a pole to the\nmean of the other corners (one side of the period), only when the\nsurface point stays within 1e-9 mm. Spline faces only.\n\nq02 now imports: 48780 facets, no open edge, 97163.50 mm^3 (SolidCraft\n97165.69), and slices at z = 19.6875.\n\nPinned by a hand-built pole fan, a quarter-sphere STEP fixture of our\nown (kernel mesh and app import + slices), and mesh_pole unit tests.\n\nFixes #3034\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
